      "id": "17862126",
      "title": "Angular Libraries - An Introduction",
      "lectureOrder": 747,
      "videoOrder": 687,
      "sourceHash": "36e36828727f83aac0f5badf0d90701bb8b161ff16bb1501df8accd70b38ec07",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.31,
          "end": 3.48,
          "en": "Instructor: To create a library,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.48,
          "end": 6.27,
          "en": "we run \"ng generate library,\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.27,
          "end": 8.01,
          "en": "an alternative to application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.01,
          "end": 9.72,
          "en": "In this case, let's say \"my-button\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.72,
          "end": 11.67,
          "en": "because it's an amazing library where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 11.67,
          "end": 14.49,
          "en": "I will share my own custom button component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 14.49,
          "end": 17.16,
          "en": "which every other application should be able to use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.16,
          "end": 19.53,
          "en": "and that's maybe important. What is a library?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 19.53,
          "end": 22.08,
          "en": "A library differs from an application such",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 22.08,
          "end": 24.36,
          "en": "that you still write Angular code in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 24.36,
          "end": 27.66,
          "en": "you still build Angular components and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 27.66,
          "end": 30.87,
          "en": "You can group them with modules, you can add directives,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 30.87,
          "end": 33.78,
          "en": "that does not change but it's not meant to run standalone",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 33.78,
          "end": 35.28,
          "en": "as a web application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 35.28,
          "end": 39.21,
          "en": "Instead, it's meant to have some code that can be shared",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 39.21,
          "end": 42.75,
          "en": "across multiple Angular web applications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 42.75,
          "end": 46.05,
          "en": "So something like Angular Material.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 46.05,
          "end": 49.02,
          "en": "Angular Material is a Angular library.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 49.02,
          "end": 51.69,
          "en": "It comes with a bunch of building components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 51.69,
          "end": 54.51,
          "en": "and you can use these components in any application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 54.51,
          "end": 58.56,
          "en": "So this is a Angular library and you can build your own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 58.56,
          "end": 60.39,
          "en": "Now, we already made our first steps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 60.39,
          "end": 63.87,
          "en": "by creating it with the ng generate library command.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 63.87,
          "end": 66.45,
          "en": "You see, you generally get the same as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 66.45,
          "end": 68.49,
          "en": "but there are some differences.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 68.49,
          "end": 71.91,
          "en": "For example, we have a \"ng-package.json\" file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 71.91,
          "end": 74.73,
          "en": "which in the end allows us to configure this library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 74.73,
          "end": 76.17,
          "en": "in a certain way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 76.17,
          "end": 80.88,
          "en": "In the source folder, we see we have a \"public-api.ts\" file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 80.88,
          "end": 83.28,
          "en": "where we in the end export different things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 83.28,
          "end": 85.77,
          "en": "that make up our library, and in the \"lib\" folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 85.77,
          "end": 87.39,
          "en": "we got some starting files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 87.39,
          "end": 89.85,
          "en": "For example, a my button component where we can",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 89.85,
          "end": 94.65,
          "en": "write our own library component, already added to a module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 94.65,
          "end": 98.75999999999999,
          "en": "And also a service, which you can or cannot use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 98.75999999999999,
          "end": 102.06,
          "en": "Now to learn all about library creation, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 102.06,
          "end": 104.88,
          "en": "as always, the official docs are your friends,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 104.88,
          "end": 107.257,
          "en": "under \"TECHNIQUES,\" \"Angular Libraries,\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 107.257,
          "end": 111.3,
          "en": "\"Creating Libraries.\" You can learn all about creating",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 111.3,
          "end": 115.14,
          "en": "and also deploying, publishing your own custom libraries",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 115.14,
          "end": 119.03999999999999,
          "en": "to npm. For that, you will also need a npm account though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 119.03999999999999,
          "end": 122.46,
          "en": "So this is in the end something you can also do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 122.46,
          "end": 125.64,
          "en": "And building a library really is straightforward.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 125.64,
          "end": 128.52,
          "en": "Here, for example, I could build my own custom button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 128.52,
          "end": 131.19,
          "en": "which of course is super amazing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 131.19,
          "end": 135.091,
          "en": "There, I will use \"ng-content,\" so that users can pass",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 135.091,
          "end": 138.39,
          "en": "in anything they want between my custom button tags",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 138.39,
          "end": 141.18,
          "en": "and that's it. So of course, the most amazing button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 141.18,
          "end": 143.85,
          "en": "in the world has no styles, no extra features,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 143.85,
          "end": 147.42000000000002,
          "en": "you absolutely need this library.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 147.42000000000002,
          "end": 150.42000000000002,
          "en": "Now, with that, we already would have a very basic library,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 150.42000000000002,
          "end": 152.31,
          "en": "which we now can configure, and again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 152.31,
          "end": 155.55,
          "en": "the official docs can help you there to learn about how",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 155.55,
          "end": 157.53,
          "en": "to exactly configure this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 157.53,
          "end": 162.24,
          "en": "And with this, we are also able to build libraries,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 162.24,
          "end": 165.93,
          "en": "and share them across either our own Angular applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 165.93,
          "end": 169.263,
          "en": "or all to publish them to npm, to share them with others.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
